Let the test driver follow a symbolic link to its fixture. Bazel hands every test input
over as a symlink into the runfiles tree, and magic_file without MAGIC_SYMLINK classifies
the link itself: every tests/Makefile.am check-local case would report "symbolic link to
..." instead of the fixture's contents. make check reads regular files, for which the flag
changes nothing.

--- a/tests/test.c
+++ b/tests/test.c
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@
 		goto bad;
 	}
 
-	ms = magic_open(flags);
+	ms = magic_open(flags | MAGIC_SYMLINK);
 	if (ms == NULL) {
 		(void)fprintf(stderr, "%s: ERROR opening MAGIC_NONE: %s\n",
 		    prog, strerror(errno));
